/home/ubuntu/pet/cast/docs/infrastructure.md:58:- **Protocol compatibility:** TUI and headless clients compare the daemon protocol recorded in `server.json` before connecting. A mismatch (including a legacy daemon without the field) leaves the daemon untouched and asks the user to run `cast server stop` before starting Cast again.
/home/ubuntu/pet/cast/docs/mcp-servers.md:64:Remote servers are connected over **Streamable HTTP** first; if the server rejects it (legacy servers answer the initialize POST with an HTTP error), cast retries once over the deprecated **HTTP+SSE** transport — so old `/sse` endpoints (e.g. Cloudflare's docs server) work with the same one-line config. Timeouts are not retried: a hung endpoint is hung on either transport.
