es scroll position; theme changes and streaming desyncs still do a full scrollback wipe\n952: - **lineChurn** — O(m·n) fallback for large edits uses Set-based comparison instead of raw block count; identical large texts no longer report false positive changes\n953: - **Input parser** — DECXCPR cursor-position responses (`\\x1b[row;colR`) explicitly dropped to prevent accidental keybinding matches\n954: \n955: ### Internal\n956: \n957: - `displayWidth` extracted to `src/ui/display-width.ts` with per-session cache\n958: - Test directories isolated to prevent parallel test collisions\n959: \n960: ## 0.6.0\n961: \n962: ### Added\n963: \n964: - **SSH tool** — run commands on remote hosts via SSH; hosts configured in `~/.cast/ssh.json` (global) or `.cast/ssh.json` (project)\n965: - `/queue-reset` alias — shortcut for clearing the command queue\n966: \n967: ## 0.5.8\n968: \n969: ### Added\n970: \n971: - MCP server toggle — `/mcp` now opens an interactive multi-select picker to enable/disable individual servers mid-session. Disabled servers are hidden from the model and persisted in settings.\n972: - `<available_mcp>` block in the system prompt — the model sees only enabled MCP servers and their tools, and will not attempt to call disabled ones.\n973: - Hermes XML tool-call parsing and recovery\n974: - Terminal desync tracking with automatic resync on focus return\n975: \n976: ## 0.5.7\n977: \n978: ### Added\n979: \n980: - Enhanced search functionality with permission handling and output notes\n981: - Improved tool name sanitization to prevent doom loops\n982: \n983: ## 0.5.6\n984: \n985: ### Fixed\n986: \n987: - Terminal tools (`plan_done`, `plan_enter`) now force-end the turn — prevents the model from keeping runs alive by rewording summaries to dodge the doom-loop detector\n988: - `plan_done` no longer echoes full plan content into model context, which invited endless \"refinement\" loops\n989: \n990: ## 0.5.5\n991: \n992: ### Added\n993: \n994: - Changelog page with ver