y scripts. |\n| `site/` | Website/documentation site. |\n| `docs/` | Documentation. |\n| `chapters/` | Tutorial/guide chapters (likely for the `learn-everything` skill). |\n| `evals/` | Evaluation harness. |\n| `wasm/` | WebAssembly source (likely for the web UI). |\n| `assets/` | Static assets (images, etc.). |\n| `.mimocode/` | Internal tooling/configuration. |\n| `.playwright-mcp/` | Playwright MCP server configuration. |\n| `.claude/` | Claude-specific configuration. |\n\n### Summary\n\n**`src/` is the sole top-level source code directory.** It is a TypeScript monolith (no `src/` sub-packages with their own `package.json` files) organized into four domains: **core** (agent logic, tools, config), **pickers** (selection UI), **ui** (terminal rendering via React/Ink), and **web** (HTTP/WebSocket server for browser-based UI). The build compiles to a single `dist/index.js` bundle, with entry points in `bin/`."
